# Bash scripts

Every Bash script must include a comment that states what the script does. Write that comment in **French**.

- Place it immediately after the shebang (or at the top if there is no shebang).
- One short block is enough: purpose, not a line-by-line walkthrough.
- Keep code, identifiers, and commit messages in their existing language; only this description comment must be French.
- When you change what the script does, update the French comment to match.

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Copie cursor/ du framework vers .cursor/ du dépôt produit (écrasement).
set -euo pipefail
```
